The site is situated in a thick Ponderosa pine forest that provides plenty of', '48.12544000000000', '-118.23087700000001', true, 'https://www.recreation.gov/permits/10064730', 'https://cdn.recreation.gov/public/2021/03/29/21/57/10064730_296459ae-0a9a-423b-8a6d-ca04e2129615_700.webp', now()),
  ('AP21825', 'McNary and Umatilla Refuge Hunt Permit', 'Fish and Wildlife Service', 'Washington', 'Plymouth', 'Waterfowl hunting at McNary and Umatilla National Wildlife Refuges attracts hunters from across the country.  The FWS provides numerous and varied hunting opportunities, ranging from seven day per week hunting to restricted days and hours to reserved blinds for disabled hunters. 
 One of the more popular opportunities provided is controlled, limited-day hunts at McNary and Umatilla on the Fee Hunting Area and McCormack Units, respectively. These hunts, limited to a certain number of hunters, are controlled through a Check Station and the charging of a day-use fee. The daily fee is $14, with hu', '45.95734089000000', '-119.30780890000000', true, 'https://www.recreation.gov/permits/AP21825', 'https://cdn.recreation.gov/public/2023/11/17/19/58/AP21825_9eeb9275-c18e-4bd8-9162-e0fb136388f4_700.webp', now()),
  ('5363636', 'Lake Georgetown Other Small Game Hunt Permits', 'US Army Corps of Engineers', null, 'Georgetown', 'Lake Georgetown is a multipurpose water resources project constructed and operated by the U.S. Army Corps of Engineers (USACE), Fort Worth District. The lake and associated federal lands are located in Williamson County, Texas (TX). Lake Georgetown Dam is situated on the San Gabriel River in the Brazos River Basin about 3.5 miles west of the City of Georgetown, TX. The dam and associated infrastructure, as well as all lands acquired for the Lake Georgetown project, are federally owned and administered by the USACE.   With over 1200 surface acres of water and 2500 acres of wildlife management a', '30.67685290282021', '-97.72065401509552', true, 'https://www.recreation.gov/permits/5363636', 'https://cdn.recreation.gov/public/2026/06/16/13/58/5363636_cc9ab108-9dcc-45a4-b2da-4324def62c41_700.jpg', now()),
  ('5353535', 'Lake Georgetown Waterfowl Hunt Permits', 'US Army Corps of Engineers', null, 'Georgetown', 'Lake Georgetown is a multipurpose water resources project constructed and operated by the U.S. Army Corps of Engineers (USACE), Fort Worth District. The lake and associated federal lands are located in Williamson County, Texas (TX). Lake Georgetown Dam is situated on the San Gabriel River in the Brazos River Basin about 3.5 miles west of the City of Georgetown, TX. The dam and associated infrastructure, as well as all lands acquired for the Lake Georgetown project, are federally owned and administered by the USACE.   With over 1200 surface acres of water and 2500 acres of wildlife management a', '30.67685290282021', '-97.72065401509552', true, 'https://www.recreation.gov/permits/5353535', 'https://cdn.recreation.gov/public/2026/07/07/20/53/5353535_2e80e061-6d4c-4e78-9f46-e9fb2822b465_700.jpg', now()),
  ('5242424', 'Tennessee Tombigbee Waterway Hunting Permit', 'US Army Corps of Engineers', null, 'Columbus', 'The U.S. Army Corps of Engineers (USACE) at the Tennessee Tombigbee Waterway (TTWW) issue annual hunting permits for the land managed by USACE along the 234 miles of project. The permits are subject to a $15.00 special activity fee that is assessed each season. TTWW Hunting Permits include permit number, name, and vehicle information. The hunting permit needs to be printed and clearly displayed on the dash of the vehicle while hunting. Hunting area maps may be viewed or obtained from the Tennessee Tombigbee Waterway website at:   https://www.sam.usace.army.mil/Missions/Civil-Works/Recreation/T', '33.53446000000000', '-88.50160300000000', true, 'https://www.recreation.gov/permits/5242424', 'https://cdn.recreation.gov/public/2024/07/24/17/38/5242424_8662c6cf-5602-4ba1-8b66-26bd410a45c7_700.webp', now())
